[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Slav Defence"]
[Variation "Exchange Variation"]
[ECO "D10"]
[Character "solid,positional"]
[Risk "low"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "none"]
[Themes "symmetrical-structure,bishop-trade"]

1. d4 d5 2. c4 c6 3. cxd5 { White trades the c-pawn, which gives a symmetrical position. } 3... cxd5 { Retakes with the c-pawn, so Black keeps a pawn on d5 and gets the open c-file. }
4. Nc3 ( 4. Nf3 Nf6 5. Nc3 Nc6 6. Bf4 Bf5 7. e3 e6 ) 4... Nf6
5. Bf4 Nc6 { Develops and adds pressure on d4. }
6. e3 Bf5 { Brings the bishop out before ...e6 closes it in. }
7. Nf3 e6 { Guards d5 and opens the bishop on f8. }
8. Bd3 Bxd3 { Trades bishops, so White cannot use the bishop on d3 to attack Black's king side. }
9. Qxd3 Bd6 { Offers a trade of White's active bishop on f4. }
10. Bxd6 Qxd6 { Retakes with the queen, which now looks at the open c-file and d-pawn. }
11. O-O O-O *
